  m_Name: PokedexFennec
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryId: fennec
  commonName: Fennec Fox
  scientificName: Vulpes zerda
  icon: {fileID: 10904, guid: 0000000000000000f000000000000000, type: 0}
  category: Mammal
  habitat: Sandy Deserts & Arid Basins
  height: 0.20 m
  weight: 1.30 kg
  diet: Omnivore
  rarity: Common
  shortDescription: The smallest of all canine species, easily distinguished by its
    exceptionally large ears and pale, sand-colored fur.
  behaviorNotes: Mainly active at night to hunt insects, rodents, and small reptiles.
    Their large ears act like sensitive tracking dishes to hear prey moving completely
    underground.
  observationTips: They are highly agile and swift. Look near underground burrow
    openings or watch for them darting quickly between desert dunes.
  funFact: Their massive ears aren't just for incredible hearing; they are packed
    with blood vessels that allow the fox to dissipate intense body heat, acting
    like a natural air conditioning system.
  facts:
  - The thick fur on the bottoms of their paws protects them from getting burned
    by the scorching desert sand.
  - They are so well-adapted to arid regions that they can go for indefinite periods
    without drinking liquid water, obtaining all necessary moisture directly from
    their prey.
  - Fennec foxes are highly social animals that live in tightly-knit family groups
    within complex, interconnected underground den networks.
